@startuml permit_state_machine
skinparam dpi 170
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #1a5f8f
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5b6b7a
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #e8f1f8
  BorderColor #1a5f8f
  FontColor #0f3d5e
  AttributeFontColor #3c4a57
  AttributeFontSize 12
  FontSize 14
  BackgroundColor<<success>> #e3f4e8
  BorderColor<<success>> #3c8d5a
  BackgroundColor<<fail>> #fbe9e9
  BorderColor<<fail>> #b94a4a
  BackgroundColor<<closed>> #f0f0f0
  BorderColor<<closed>> #5b6b7a
}
hide stereotype

title YatraPass — Permit State Machine

state ACTIVE <<success>> : Valid from start date to end date\n(inclusive, Asia/Kathmandu time)\nQR scans can return VALID
state EXPIRED <<closed>> : Scan returns PERMIT_EXPIRED
state CANCELLED <<fail>> : Reason recorded\nScan returns PERMIT_CANCELLED
state COMPLETED : Trip finished\nScan returns PERMIT_NOT_ACTIVE

[*] --> ACTIVE : Application approved\n/ permit number PRM-YYYY-NNNNNN\n/ QR token generated
ACTIVE --> EXPIRED : Scheduler (daily 00:05)\n[end date has passed]
ACTIVE --> CANCELLED : Admin cancels\n[reason given]
ACTIVE --> COMPLETED : Admin marks completed
ACTIVE --> ACTIVE : Admin regenerates QR\n/ old token REVOKED,\nnew token issued
EXPIRED --> [*]
CANCELLED --> [*]
COMPLETED --> [*]

note left of ACTIVE
  Verification also checks dates directly,
  so a permit is never reported VALID
  after its end date, even before the
  expiry job has run.
end note

note bottom of CANCELLED
  EXPIRED, CANCELLED and COMPLETED are terminal.
  Any other change is refused with HTTP 409.
end note
@enduml
